# p_d4c8 — Couple with staggered errands; receptacle_19 cluster rotates in and out

Two adults live here. Both work, but on different schedules: one is home by 08:00, the other leaves later (around 10:00) and returns around 16:00. This staggered pattern means that during the 09:00–17:00 window, one resident is always present (explaining why object_2 and object_35 are found 3/4 times at receptacle_11) while the other's personal items are out.

The key distinguishing feature of this document is the receptacle_19 cluster. Objects object_5, object_6, object_7, object_9, object_12, object_19, and object_23 are all "mostly" at receptacle_19, yet none of them was found there during weekday 9–17 h looks (0/4 for each). They are present at receptacle_19 on some days (mornings, evenings, weekends) but absent during weekday midday. This document predicts they are taken out by the later-leaving resident on errands or to a second workplace, and return in the evening.

The very stable objects (object_29 at receptacle_22, object_30 at receptacle_16, object_34 at receptacle_21, object_27/31 at receptacle_6) are household fixtures that never move. object_1 is at receptacle_17 mornings and evenings but out during weekday midday (0/3 found), consistent with the later-leaving resident carrying it.

